WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:00.980
Also, where should I look?

00:02.500 --> 00:03.700
My name is Sage Cadence.

00:03.920 --> 00:06.880
I'm a Stanford electrical engineering student who loves to build hardware.

00:07.840 --> 00:08.240
Sorry.

00:08.620 --> 00:10.220
That I also share on the internet.

00:10.380 --> 00:10.820
Hi, friends.

00:11.000 --> 00:12.660
Here's how I built a beating heart circuit board.

00:12.840 --> 00:14.140
This is how to build an engineering project.

00:14.240 --> 00:15.440
Make your first circuit board with me.

00:17.880 --> 00:20.960
So I have these two star-shaped circuit boards.

00:21.140 --> 00:22.360
The first lights up in the dark.

00:22.520 --> 00:24.180
The second is a portable voice diary.

00:24.360 --> 00:25.520
And the third is a secret.

00:25.760 --> 00:29.180
Before Devin Bots, the process of building a circuit board like this would take a long time

00:29.180 --> 00:31.280
because I have to build it and then check it.

00:31.680 --> 00:34.880
Devin Bots really trims down the time to success.

00:35.360 --> 00:36.620
Look, it's already done.

00:36.820 --> 00:39.920
The only difference is that now I have a few more hands to help me make it happen.

00:40.160 --> 00:41.240
Meet my Devin Bots.

00:41.460 --> 00:47.260
One is constantly researching for new components, parts that I haven't seen before, new ways to do things.

00:47.420 --> 00:50.160
Another one can work on the firmware while I'm actually building the thing.

00:50.320 --> 00:52.020
Another one is constantly checking my work.

00:52.160 --> 00:57.000
It allows me to try much more ambitious projects while learning, while focusing on the parts that I enjoy.

00:57.000 --> 00:59.660
It's kind of like having a little engineering team of my own.
